# @kp-soft/themes v1.2.0 — the release's own SHA256SUMS, mapped onto
# kyu's flat static/ paths. Fetched with:
#   gh release download v1.2.0 --repo kennypassenier/kp-themes -p SHA256SUMS -O -
#
# Why a recorded copy rather than a live fetch: this is checked by the
# commit gate, and a gate that needs the network fails on a train. These
# hashes say 'our six copies are unmodified AND are the tag we claim' —
# a claim that holds offline and does not depend on what happens to be
# in a sibling directory. Bumping the version means re-copying the files
# AND refreshing this file, which is exactly the deliberate act it
# should be.
#
# no-flash.js joined the list at v1.2.0. It is the only one here the
# browser never fetches: kyu inlines its NO_FLASH_SNIPPET into the
# document head, because a module arrives too late to prevent the flash
# it exists to prevent. It is vendored so a test can compare what
# layout.html inlines against the package's own text, and so this gate
# notices when that text changes upstream.
